# Files that start a process themselves (tools/check-process-starts.py, docs/PROCESSES.md):
# <path> <count of lines found> <reason>

# The two helpers.
crates/appkit-core/src/child.rs 2 the helper for children of the app
crates/appkit-core/src/launch.rs 2 the helper for a program of somebody else (it outlives the hub on purpose)

# Named exceptions that stay (decided 2026-11-14): Neovim as the editor in a visible console of its own, a window the person asked for and works in; a link handed to the system (ShellExecuteW) starts no process of the app.
crates/appkit-hub/src/browser.rs 2 hands a link to the default browser (ShellExecuteW; open and xdg-open go through launch)
crates/appkit-hub/src/editor.rs 3 named exception: Neovim in a visible console (Windows) or in a terminal program (Linux)

# Named exception that stays: the hub puts itself in the background (a case of its own, not a child of an app). Its call of reg.exe is a system tool that is replaced by a task of its own.
crates/appkit-hub/src/background.rs 4 named exception: the hub in the background; reg.exe is replaced later
crates/appkit-core/src/registry.rs 2 icacls.exe on the secret file (no window), a blocking call that has not moved to the helper yet

# A test program (it plays a child that starts a process of its own).
crates/appkit-testkit/src/bin/child-probe.rs 3 the probe of the child tests (a grandchild, the control start of a hub without a console, a start without standard handles)
